Subject: [PATCH 14/19] Establish that the seed needs one subscription month a
 year, not twelve

The measured rule is that a seed must be contemporaneous with the margins it
fits, which is not the same as paying every month.  Two checks settle the
difference: a query 379 days back returns no flights, so the archive reaches
365 days; and AFAC's July 2026 bulletin already reports July 2026, so a newly
published month falls well inside that window with about ten months to spare.

So the backlog can be pulled in one paid month and the subscription cancelled,
repeated annually before the oldest months age out: USD 19 to 57 a year against
USD 19 a month.

The same window is a deadline.  Everything before September 2025 is already
outside it and cannot be bought back later -- including 2024M01 to 2025M03,
which is exactly the span of AFAC margins already in the repository.  Only a
provider with a deep archive can reach those, and only for backfill.

Flag the untested assumption the cheaper figure rests on: that one full week
fixes a month's carrier mix.  It is measurable for free inside the first paid
month by comparing a one-week seed against a thirty-day one.

